From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] deckcraft: the command hook also guards pointer gestures, and the notes and outline fields can be held inert

A policy that bars edits (a read-only session) must stop a change before it shows, not take it back a frame later. Commands
already ask the hook; two paths did not. Pointer gestures (drag, resize, rotate, draw, ink) change the presentation through
Session::edit with no command, so Session::edit and the press of a drawing tool now ask the hook for the UI-level name
office_hook::EDIT ("doc.edit"). The notes pane, the notes page and the outline are egui text fields that show typed text before
a command runs, so SlideApp::locked() (the hook refuses EDIT) makes them non-interactive. With no hook nothing changes.
Test: crates/engine/tests/office_hook.rs.
---

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/lib.rs b/crates/engine/src/lib.rs
index 942262c..57c964e 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/lib.rs
@@ -656,6 +656,10 @@ impl Session {
 
     /// Mutate the active presentation (copy-on-write) and bump the revision.
     pub fn edit<T>(&mut self, f: impl FnOnce(&mut Presentation, &mut Selection) -> Result<T>) -> Result<T> {
+        // The pointer tools change the presentation here without a command; a policy that bars edits refuses them too.
+        if let Some(why) = office_hook::refusal(office_hook::EDIT, self) {
+            return Err(EngineError::Disabled(office_hook::EDIT.into(), why));
+        }
         let st = self.doc_mut()?;
         let mut doc = (*st.doc).clone();
         let mut sel = st.selection.clone();
